    45	
    46	The head-SHA run list contains UNRELATED runs, **including the npm-publish
    47	run doing the asking**. Non-candidate runs are IGNORED — never BLOCK.
    48	"Mismatch" is only ever evaluated against the exact candidate
    49	(workflow + tag + SHA + event). If any near-miss run could BLOCK, every
    50	release would lose the race against its own presence in the list.
    51	
    52	## Freshness (delete + re-tag of the SAME sha)
    53	
    54	Re-tagging the same commit leaves the OLD Release run in the list with the
    55	same ``head_sha``/``head_branch``. Polling before the NEW Release run is
    56	created would otherwise find the old ``success`` as "most recent" and grant
    57	— even if the new run later fails. So a candidate must have been created no
    58	earlier than the asking run's own creation, minus ``--freshness-skew-seconds``
    59	(default 120s) to absorb same-push jitter: both workflows are created by one
    60	push event, and their ``created_at`` ordering is arbitrary within seconds.
    61	Runs older than that window are not candidates at all (→ WAIT, then BLOCK at
    62	the deadline). KNOWN LIMIT, stated rather than hidden: a delete+re-tag
    63	completed FASTER than the skew window can still admit the previous run; the
    64	skew is a jitter allowance, not a proof, and it is printed with every
    65	decision so the value used is auditable.
    66	
    67	``--self-created-at`` is REQUIRED. It is the input that switches this whole
    68	leg on, so it gets no default: omitting it (or passing an empty/unparseable
    69	value) is a usage error (exit 2), never a run that silently grants stale
    70	successes. Same doctrine as ``_release_bump_sites.py --today``: a parameter
    71	that changes the verdict has no default. The doctrine holds at BOTH layers:
    72	``GateContext.self_created_at_epoch`` is likewise a required field with no
    73	default (and an explicit ``None`` raises), so an in-process caller of
    74	``decide()`` cannot construct a context with the freshness leg silently off.
